  "failure_explanations": [
    "Baseline running-but-hung supervisor did not recover before implementation.",
    "Initial peer candidate failed its quiet audit because healthy launchctl polling generated spurious inspection failures. Current code checks live progress/executable locally and invokes launchctl only for stale/missing progress.",
    "Two early mode assertions sampled status=refreshing before the terminal ready snapshot. Harness now waits for ready plus blocked/address; monitoring services were running in captured states.",
    "Activate failed health verification because the Stop receipt correctly blocked peer repair of the missing heartbeat. Installer now explicitly starts both peers before verification and retains the receipt until success; regression failed before the fix, then installed lifecycle passed.",
    "A real startup provider rate limit caused the zero-error audit to fail. The audit now requires exactly one rate-limit pause, one provider rotation and one subsequent success, with exactly two completed lookups. Quiet-window checks remain unchanged.",
    "The initial candidate package also failed PF parent inspection once. Added bounded command/inspection diagnostics; later normal package installs succeeded. That first occurrence was not conclusively attributed."
